      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-16T13:57:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We use this hooks to record runtime irq number in DDR memory, not in panic process.",
      "parentUuid": "3d87623c_4775149d",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4317ef07_e539b393",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-16T14:05:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "irq numbers are already available in userspace, no need to hook every single irq twice, that is going to be a huge performance impact for no real gain as the information can be gotten elsewhere (i.e. your drivers know the irq numbers for themselves, have them save that information in the panic log if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "8370fea0_4678b659",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2cf9209_f426fb3d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3358448
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-17T06:49:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s too late to acquire irq number in userspace when system panic in kernelspace. This solution has already been tested on our platform, and the time cost is acceptable. When system panic, we dump the memory to see whether interruption storm happended and which irq entered but not exit.\nIt\u0027s not a good solution to modify every driver\u0027s code to record irq number. Also, native kernel driver code cannot be modified.",
      "parentUuid": "4317ef07_e539b393",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74f88e2e_f9e4572e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-17T07:51:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You know, at boot time, the irqs that are assigned to all devices, save that information then, no need to do so each irq, that will have a performance impact",
      "parentUuid": "a2cf9209_f426fb3d",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfc9f2fb_5d49da41",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3358448
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-17T08:52:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We use these hooks to record the interrupt enter and exit, not to save the irq number of all devices. We will not register hook handler in user version, just in eng version.",
      "parentUuid": "74f88e2e_f9e4572e",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a0095ad_dc361620",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125653
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-17T09:11:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In eng version you do not have to use the gki kernel, please just put this type of change there.  It is a VERY dangerous hook to have, I do not recommend it be present at all, sorry.\n\nAnd again, you have this information (irq number) in userspace, trying to log every irq at runtime is an impossible task that is not really useful at all.  Do so in the drivers you think have problems if you really want to.",
      "parentUuid": "bfc9f2fb_5d49da41",
      "revId": "5b4ef09d26581f7fb55f6da803780eb39534964c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
